    "content": "Approximate Writing Pattern Review Reviews up to 2,500 characters for repetitive, uniform, or robotic patterns and returns an overall guidance label. Reviews writing for robotic or repetitive patterns and returns approximate guidance. Human-written text can be flagged, so results are not proof of authorship. Highlights passages that may benefit from more variation, specificity, clarity, or voice. Results are guidance, not proof of authorship. AI Content Detector reviews writing for repetitive, formulaic, or robotic patterns. It does not determine whether a person or AI wrote the text. Its result is an approximate editorial signal that can help you find passages that may need more variety, specificity, or voice. The review uses strict pattern thresholds. Human-written text can be flagged, especially when it is short, technical, templated, highly edited, or uses repeated sentence structures. AI-assisted text can also appear natural after editing. Always use your own judgment. • Repeated phrasing and similar sentence structures • Predictable flow or generic language • Limited variation, weak transitions, or thin explanations • Passages that may benefit from examples, context, or a clearer voice Use highlighted passages as editing prompts. Add specifics, explain the reasoning, vary sentence structure, remove filler, and make the wording fit the intended audience. The goal is clearer, more useful writing, not to pass or defeat a detector. Results are approximate and can be wrong. They do not verify authorship and should not be used as proof in academic, employment, legal, or disciplinary decisions. A strong robotic-writing signal means the text matched more of the review’s patterns. It does not mean AI wrote the text. Writers, editors, marketers, students, educators, and content teams can use the review as one input in a broader editorial process. Compare the guidance with the source, context, and your own judgment before deciding what to change. Small, focused utilities for recurring knowledge work and everyday operations. No. It reviews writing patterns and returns an approximate signal. Human writing can be flagged, and edited AI-assisted writing may not be flagged. The review uses strict pattern thresholds. Short, technical, templated, repetitive, or highly edited human writing can match those patterns. Use it as one editorial input. Review the highlighted passages, consider the source and context, and apply your own judgment. Do not use the result as proof of authorship or as the sole basis for a consequential decision. You can review text from any source. The source does not change the tool's purpose: it looks for writing patterns that may benefit from editing. Yes. The submitted text is sent through the Moxby gateway to the analysis service. Do not submit confidential or sensitive text unless your use complies with your organization's policies. No reviews yet. Reviews require a verified Marketplace package install or a signed extension release for this Mod. Explore related products or browse the complete Productivity category. 3 products Compare the product type, required plan, compatibility, and publisher before adding it to Moxby. Adds a polished fixed sidebar on Google Search pages listing result titles as links so results are visible without scrolling the full page. View product Pages, spreadsheets, boards, lists, calendars, and task planning inside Moxby. View product Turn meeting material into decisions, owners, action items, and unresolved questions. View product Looking for more Productivity products? View category Chat on any page, build Mods, run Missions, and add ready-made products from the Marketplace.",
