ngle verdict. Sign in only when you want to save it to your dossier or cite it externally. Drop audio. Paste a URL, drag a file, or record straight from the page. Accepts MP3, WAV, M4A, WebM up to 25MB. The model listens. Roughly half a second of compute. We run the clip against 24+ generator signatures and return a probability, not a label. Get the notice. A permanent, citable verdict with confidence, attribution, and a methodology link. Quote it. Subpoena it. File it. Twenty-four generators, named. Every major voice synthesis system in production. New entrants added the month they ship. Methodology version stamped on every verdict. What you get vs. listening twice. The human ear is unreliable on current-generation synthesis. The detector returns a citable probability with a published method behind it. Capability Listening twice Generic AI detector aivoicedetector.com Verdict speed Minutes 2-5 seconds 0.48s median Accuracy on clean audio ~60% 85-92% 99% Model attribution No Sometimes 24+ generators named Citable output No No Permanent URL + APA Methodology published N/A Rare Versioned monthly Audio retention N/A 30-90 days 24 hours, fingerprint after Free tier Free Sometimes 50 a month, no card Put the verdict in your stack. The same model behind one REST endpoint. POST an audio clip, get a citable probability with model attribution in under half a second. Webhooks for bulk, JSON in and out. Explore the API → We don't think AI voices are going to slow down. We think the open web needs a single, citable instrument for asking \"is this real?\" and getting an answer with receipts. We retrain monthly. We publish our methodology. Every verdict is permanent and quotable. No black box, no marketing budget. Just the model, kept current, and the team behind it answering email. Questions we hear often. If yours is not here, email the team. Reply within the day, every day. How accurate is the detector? How long does a clip need to be? What happens to my audio? Can I cite this