    "official_url": "https://arobis.ai/ai-visibility-checker",
    "source": "https://arobis.ai/ai-visibility-checker",
    "content": "See how often ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, Perplexity and Copilot recommend your brand. Enter your domain, get your AI Visibility Score and the fixes that matter, in about 60 seconds. No signup. It runs your domain against the signals AI engines use when they decide which brands to name. You get an AI Visibility Score, a breakdown of where you are weak, and a prioritized list of fixes. It is a diagnostic, not a rank tracker: it tells you why AI engines are leaving you out before you spend money trying to change it. Enter your domain in the checker above. No account and no credit card. The checker reads your entity signals, structured data, content answerability and llms.txt status, then returns your AI Visibility Score with a ranked list of fixes. Work the list from the top, then re-check in about a month. The score combines entity clarity, structured data, content answerability, llms.txt readiness and the third-party sources that corroborate your brand. A low score almost never means your product is weak. It usually means the web does not describe you clearly enough for a model to repeat it with confidence. ChatGPT, Google Gemini, Claude, Perplexity and Microsoft Copilot. Classic search visibility is part of the picture too, because Google indexation underpins AI Overviews and Bing underpins Copilot, so the checker doubles as a search engine visibility checker for the layer that feeds AI answers. The free checker is automated and instant, and it tells you what is broken on your own site. An AI Visibility Audit goes further: we run real buyer prompts across the engines, record which competitors get named instead of you, and map the sources those answers cite. Start with the checker. Book the audit when you want to know what buyers are actually being told. An AI visibility check tests how often AI engines (ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, Perplexity and Copilot) mention, cite and recommend your brand when people ask them for solutions in your category. It measures your presence inside AI answers, not your position on a classic search results page. Yes. The checker is free and starts without a signup. You enter your domain and get your AI Visibility Score and recommended fixes in about 60 seconds. Five engines: ChatGPT, Google Gemini, Claude, Perplexity and Microsoft Copilot, the platforms where most AI-driven product discovery happens today. The score combines the signals AI engines rely on when choosing which brands to cite: entity clarity, structured data, content answerability, llms.txt readiness and the citation sources that corroborate your brand. A higher score means engines can understand, trust and recommend you more easily. Yes. Classic search visibility feeds AI answers, because Google indexation underpins AI Overviews and Bing underpins Copilot, so the check covers that layer as part of your AI footprint. Fix the gaps the checker finds: clarify your entity, add clean schema markup, publish answer-ready content, add an llms.txt file and earn mentions on the sources AI engines read, such as review platforms, comparison posts and industry lists. llms.txt is a plain-text file that tells AI crawlers what your site is about and which pages matter most. Think robots.txt, but written for language models. The checker flags whether you have one. Monthly, or after any significant site change. AI models refresh continuously and competitors actively work on their own visibility, so a score from three months ago is stale. Most free AI visibility tools track mentions over time. This checker is diagnostic: it evaluates your website's readiness to be cited and tells you what to fix first, which is the step before tracking makes sense.",
