    "source": "https://www.gatsbi.com/",
    "content": "Meet your next‑gen AI research assistant. Discover original research ideas and draft academic paper manuscripts; screen and synthesize literature; and run systematic reviews and meta‑analyses — all in one place. Download Gatsbi Download for Windows Windows 10/11 Download for macOS Apple Silicon Web Version Enjoy a 1-day free trial. — Limited time offer with selected features. No payment method needed. Your browser does not support the video tag. Discover Original Research Ideas: Input your research topic, and Gatsbi detects research gaps and generates innovative solutions. Write Academic Papers: Gatsbi auto-drafts paper manuscripts with citations and figures, based on your research notes or prior materials. Run SLRs & Meta‑Analyses: Gatsbi screens, extracts, and synthesizes literature, and generates analytical dimensions, plots and calculations. Patent Your Inventions: Gatsbi drafts structured patent disclosure materials in 11 languages for review by qualified patent professionals. PRODUCT FEATURES Powerful Features Tailored for Researchers and Innovators AI for Research Idea Discovery Input your research topic or domain and let Gatsbi generate 10+ innovative ideas and detailed solutions with originality scores and relevant references, mimicking a human research workflow. One-click generation of fully formatted research paper drafts with equations, figures, in-text citations, and real references, covering methodological, experimental, case-study, and mixed-methods research. Starting with Gatsbi 3.0, we introduced an integrated Deep Research Agent that automatically collects and synthesizes evidence to support your research. Accelerate systematic literature reviews and meta-analyses with AI-powered study screening, data extraction, statistical synthesis, and editable review results before manuscript writing. Optionally import a self-maintained Zotero literature list for systematic review or meta-analysis writing. Prepare structured patent disclosure drafts, including technical background, invention details, embodiments, drawing explanations, and preliminary claim language, based on generated concepts or your prior research for professional review. Gatsbi Innovator helps you discover innovative research ideas in science and engineering — generate hypotheses, explore implementation or modeling details, and identify novelty before drafting your paper manuscript or patent disclosure. Powering 100,000+ Researchers and Innovators in 150+ Countries In the fast-evolving world of XR, staying ahead requires constant innovation, and Gatsbi has been instrumental in elevating our creative process. Its AI-powered insights and adaptability have unlocked new possibilities, helping us design groundbreaking immersive experiences. Gatsbi doesn't just assist our work—it propels us to shape the future of XR. Chi Xu, PhD XREAL Inc., CEO Gatsbi has been a game-changer for our team, driving rapid ideation and innovation across Al algorithms, automated control systems, and mechanicaldesign. lts versatility and intelligence have streamlined our workflow, savingus time while empowering us to break new ground in innovation. Truly acatalyst for groundbreaking ideas and technological progress! Jack Cai, PhD Sigma Squares Tech, CEO Gatsbi has revolutionized the way we approach innovation, seamlessly integrating AI to spark creativity and drive new ideas. Its intelligent design and adaptability empower our team to think bigger, move faster, and achieve more. Gatsbi doesn't just support innovation—it inspires it, becoming an essential partner in our journey to redefine possibilities. Wei Zheng, PhD Web3 Startup Founder PRICING PLANS Plans that match your needs！ Transparent pricing with no hidden fees. Cancel anytime. Unlimited monthly usage. To use Gatsbi, you need to first create an account and then purchase a subscription. Gatsbi is a desktop application, so you need to download and install it on your computer. Once you have installed Gatsbi, you can start using it by logging in with your account. To write a research paper manuscript or patent disclosure draft with Gatsbi, you will need 3 simple steps: Input your research topic, and let Gatsbi generate a list of innovative ideas; Select one idea you like, and click the 'Expand' button to get a detailed implementation of the idea; Click the 'Write a Paper Manuscript' or 'Write a Patent Disclosure' button to generate your paper or patent, respectively. For a more detailed guide, please refer to our Tutorial. Why is Gatsbi the best AI for research? Gatsbi supports key stages of the research workflow, from ideation to manuscript drafting, combining AI-assisted innovation discovery, academic writing, citations, figures, equations, and structured research outputs. What types of research papers can Gatsbi help draft? Gatsbi supports drafting several types of research manuscripts, including methodological papers, experimental research papers, case studies, systematic literature reviews, and meta-analyses. It helps organize research arguments, summarize evidence, present results, and structure manuscripts for further review and revision. How do I activate my free trial? Create an account or sign in to User Space, then launch Gatsbi Web Version. You can also download the desktop app and sign in there. In either flow, Gatsbi will show a screen where you can activate the Trial. The Trial gives you 1 day of free access, does not require a payment method, and will not automatically charge you when it expires. Trial limits: Trial users cannot export generated documents. Trial users cannot use the meta-analysis feature. Trial users cannot use Plugin features. All other features are available to try for free during the Trial. What is the technology behind Gatsbi? Gatsbi is based on a complex agentic workflow that orchestrates multiple AI agents to assist in the innovation process. However, its detailed implementation is confidential as part of our intellectual property. Which Al model does Gatsbi use at the backend? Gatsbi is not based on a single model. It orchestrates different AI models (e.g., different versions of ChatGPT or a hybrid of Qwen, DeepSeek, etc.) to optimize the balance between capabilities and costs. This multi-model approach allows us to deliver the best performance while maintaining affordable cost. Who should use Gatsbi? Gatsbi is designed for a wide range of users, including researchers, engineers, enterprises, and innovation teams. Whether you're a researcher drafting research manuscripts, an engineer developing innovative solutions, or an enterprise team managing patent documentation, Gatsbi's AI-powered tools can streamline your workflow and enhance productivity. Its comprehensive features support everything from ideation to structured documentation, making it valuable for academic, research, technical, and innovation work. Do you record users activities? For monthly and yearly Pro users, if you use the desktop version, we do not record any of your usage activities—your entire history is stored locally on your device. If you use the web version, your history is encrypted and stored on our cloud servers. We do not access your activity unless you explicitly authorize us to do so to resolve technical issues. However, in both cases, your queries are sent to third-party AI service providers (such as OpenAI). Does Gatsbi have a web version? Yes, The Gatsbi web version is now available to Pro users. Simply log in to your user space, and you can access it from the left menu bar. I'm already a subscribed member. Will the price increase and new features from this upgrade affect me? As long as you keep your subscription active, you will continue to be charged at your original rate each billing cycle. You'll also retain full access to all current member features and benefits. What are Plugin Credits? Plugin Credits are a special currency used to access Gatsbi’s advanced add-on features—such as the Humanizer plugin. They do not affect your core Gatsbi subscription, which includes the Writer and Innovator tools. Do Plugin Credits affect my Gatsbi Writer or Innovator usage? No. Plugin Credits are only used for plugin features, such as the Humanizer. All core features—paper generation, ideation, references, visuals—remain fully accessible with your subscription.",
    "source_matches_official_url": true
  },
