    "source": "https://www.libertify.com/",
    "content": "Every document. Understood. Libertify turns proposals, fund reports, policies, training and educational materials into interactive experiences that drive and measure understanding. Companies don't have a content problem. They have an understanding problem. A proposal that decides a deal. A policy that prevents a fine. A training that prevents an incident. A course that decides who graduates. These aren't documents to be opened. They're documents to be understood. The proposal goes silent. You don't know why. The buyer who didn't grasp your pricing won't ask. They'll just stop replying. The deal closes for the competitor whose proposal they actually understood. The audit finds the clause they didn't understand. Your team clicked \"I agree.\" Nobody read past page 3. When the auditor asks about clause 12, the signature you have isn't the proof you need. The incident happens. Then you find out what didn't stick. Completion hit 100% in your LMS. Then someone made the mistake the training was designed to prevent. You find out from the incident report what wasn't actually learned. The student drops out. You never saw the drift coming. Lecture views look normal. Assignments come in on time. Then they go quiet, miss deadlines, or never come back from break. Disengagement is the leading indicator: your LMS tells you who left, not who was about to. What if comprehension was something you could actually measure? See who it's for Built for teams whose documents are high-stakes. You already have the documents. What is missing is the layer between content and understanding. Don't see your use case? Talk to us → How customers use Libertify. Multilingual newsletter videos — produced at scale, on their own brand. Generali Investments runs The Euro Bond Espresso — a regular video series where their fund managers explain market views directly to clients. Libertify produces each episode across 3 languages, with 7 different speakers, using voice cloning and the executives' own photos. Three steps to turn every document into proof of understanding Upload your document. Libertify makes it interactive. Libertify makes it interactive. Add any proposal, report, policy, or training document. Libertify turns it into a guided experience that gets understood, not just opened. Works with PDF, PowerPoint, and Word, no rebuild needed Fits proposals, reports, policies, and training material alike Live in under three minutes Static PDF. AI document experience. Drag the slider to see what Libertify does to the documents you send today. Anti-Money Laundering Compliance Training Prepared by Compliance & Risk · 2025 Annual Certification 1.Detecting Suspicious Activity All employees in client-facing or transaction-processing roles are required to complete annual AML certification. Failure to identify and report suspicious activity exposes the firm to regulatory sanctions, criminal liability under the Bank Secrecy Act, and reputational damage that can take years to repair. Common red flags include unusually large cash deposits inconsistent with the client's stated occupation, rapid movement of funds between unrelated accounts, structuring transactions just below reporting thresholds, and reluctance to provide standard KYC documentation. Each pattern must be escalated to the MLRO within 24 hours of detection. Suspicious Activity Reports (SARs) must be filed within 30 days of initial detection. The filing window cannot be extended without written authorization from the Chief Compliance Officer. Do not notify the customer that a SAR has been filed: tipping off is a separate criminal offence under both UK and EU law. Individual employees may be held personally liable for failures to report. Under the Sixth Anti-Money Laundering Directive, individuals can face up to four years imprisonment for negligent non-compliance. Annual certification confirms you have read, understood, and will apply these procedures. Anti-Money Laundering Compliance Training Prepared by Compliance & Risk · 2025 Annual Certification 1. Detecting Suspicious Activity All employees in client-facing or transaction-processing roles are required to complete annual AML certification. Failure to identify and report suspicious activity exposes the firm to regulatory sanctions, criminal liability under the Bank Secrecy Act, and reputational damage. Common red flags include unusually large cash deposits inconsistent with the client's stated occupation, rapid movement of funds between unrelated accounts, and structuring transactions just below reporting thresholds. Suspicious Activity Reports (SARs) must be filed within 30 days of detection. Do not notify the customer that a SAR has been filed: tipping off is a separate criminal offence under both UK and EU law. Have a conversation with this document Ask anything about the AML Compliance Training Seeing is believing. 90 seconds One layer. Two sides of the same document. What your readers experience, and what comes back to you. AI video walkthrough A guided reading of the document, narrated. Smart highlights Key passages surfaced so nothing critical gets missed. In‑document AI assistant Readers ask questions, grounded only in the document. Learning add-ons Audio, summaries, quizzes, flashcards, notes. Multi‑language reading The same document, in the reader's language. Your brand, end to end Logo, colors, fonts, domain. It feels like yours. AI question log What readers didn't understand. Verbatim. Reading and video heatmaps Where attention held. Where it dropped. Conversation intelligence Not just what they asked. What they meant. Per‑recipient profiles See exactly what each reader did. Alerts and next moves Know the moment. Know the move. CRM, API and webhooks Pipe the signals into where you already work. Enterprise-grade security Trusted by Fortune 500 companies with the strictest security requirements. SOC 2 TYPE 2 Make your next document understood. Upload any document. See exactly what your readers understood, where they got stuck, and what they asked. Things teams ask before using Libertify. A few answers before turning your proposals, fund reports, policies and training into measurable comprehension signals. \n Libertify is the document intelligence layer. We turn the proposals, fund reports, policies, training and other documents your business sends into interactive AI experiences for readers, and surface the analytics that actually matter: not just who opened them, but who understood them, where they got stuck, and what they asked. \n Anything in PDF, PowerPoint or Word format. Customers use Libertify on sales proposals, fund factsheets, IR updates, M&A teasers, compliance policies, onboarding packs, SOPs, training modules and certification courses. If it's a high-stakes document where comprehension matters, Libertify works on it. \n Most document tools tell you a file was opened or viewed. Libertify tells you what your readers understood: which sections engaged them, where they got stuck, what questions they had, and what to do next. We don't replace your CRM, LMS or content tools. We add the missing intelligence layer that turns every document send into a measurable signal. \n The signals that matter: who opened, which sections were re-read, where readers paused or dropped off, what questions they asked the AI assistant, whether key sections were skipped, and which readers shared it internally. Every send becomes a decision: who to follow up with, what to fix, what's working. \n When a reader opens your Libertify experience, they can ask questions directly inside the document. The assistant answers only from your document content, never from external sources, and never makes things up. Every question becomes a signal: showing your team what readers cared about, what wasn't clear, or where their reasoning is heading. \n Yes. Libertify is transparent by design. Readers see a clean, branded experience with an AI assistant and guided content. We do not use hidden fingerprinting or surveillance-style tracking. The signals come from normal engagement: navigation, time spent, sections viewed, re-opens, and questions asked through the assistant. \n Yes. Libertify is designed to bring comprehension signals into your existing workflow. We integrate with sales tools (HubSpot, Salesforce), learning systems (SCORM-ready LMS platforms), and BI platforms via export and API. Engagement and comprehension data lives in your stack, not trapped inside a separate document tool. \n Yes. Libertify is SOC 2 secured. Your documents stay private to your account, and your content is never used to train external AI models. For enterprise and regulated buyers, we offer SSO, audit logs, granular permissions, GDPR compliance, and data residency options. Talk to our team if you have specific procurement requirements. Still have questions? Talk to our team → Convert any document to an interactive video experience directly from your browser.",
