annel, publishing a doc. Read-only lookups from approved sources just happen. No. Your DMs, email, calendar, and meetings stay yours. The shared Lindy sticks to approved team sources, and personal context never appears in a channel. Plans start at $29.99 per user per month with 3,000 credits. Pro and Max add more credits and more connected inboxes. Enterprise adds SSO, SCIM, audit logs, and HIPAA with a signed BAA. See full pricing. The first time someone @mentions Lindy in your Slack, they get a week free before their seat converts to paid. Admins are emailed the moment anyone joins, with a one-click link to remove them. Seats added by signing up directly are billed right away. Credits are how Lindy measures work, and bigger jobs use more. Every seat adds its allocation to one pool the whole workspace shares. If the pool runs low, Lindy pauses with a clear message, and admins can top up at $10 per 1,000 or set per-person spend caps. See full pricing. No. Your data is never sold and never used for training. Lindy is SOC 2 and GDPR compliant, and Enterprise adds HIPAA with a signed BAA. SOC 2 Type II, GDPR, HIPAA, and PIPEDA, encrypted in transit and at rest. Your data is never sold and never used to train a model, ours or anyone else's. Enterprise adds a signed BAA and audit logs. Plenty. It can't see a channel you haven't added it to or a tool you haven't connected. It won't send anything with consequences without your approval. More questions? See our docs",
