    "source": "https://www.mailmodo.com/ai-prompts/",
    "content": "AI Prompt Library Best AI ChatGPT Prompts for Marketers Explore the best AI ChatGPT prompts for marketers to plan campaigns, write faster, and boost results across SEO, content, ads, and more. Prompt #1Create a marketing strategy for a seasonal campaign Write a seasonal marketing plan for \"<insert occasion or holiday>\" to boost sales for \"<insert product or service>\". Include promotional ideas and timing. Prompt #2Build a marketing funnel for lead generation Design a 3-stage marketing funnel for \"<insert service or product>\" with content and campaign ideas for top, middle, and bottom of the funnel. Prompt #3Write a value proposition for a product Write a concise and persuasive value proposition for \"<insert product or service>\". Highlight the unique benefits and how it solves a key customer pain point. Prompt #4Write brand messaging guidelines Develop brand messaging guidelines for \"<insert company>\", including tone of voice, tagline, elevator pitch, and key messages for different audiences. Prompt #5Generate an engaging video hook (first 10 seconds) You are a YouTube SEO expert. Write a compelling video hook (first 1–2 lines of the script) for a YouTube video titled '<title>' and keyword ‘<keyword>’.\n It should grab attention within the first 10 seconds, include the keyword naturally, and set clear expectations for the viewer.\n Prompt #6Personalize a cold outreach email for a target account Write a highly personalized cold email to reach out to '<insert company name>', addressing their industry challenges and positioning '<insert product/service>' as a tailored solution. Prompt #7Write an email sequence for a high-value ABM lead Create a 3-email ABM sequence targeting '<insert company>', with each email focusing on a specific pain point and tailored value proposition of '<insert product>'. Prompt #8Suggest ABM content ideas for a specific industry Suggest 5 content ideas (e.g., case studies, ebooks, webinars) for engaging target accounts in the '<insert industry>' using account-based marketing. Prompt #9Generate a SWOT analysis for a brand Create a SWOT analysis (Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, Threats) for \"<insert brand>\" from a marketing perspective. Prompt #10Create a timestamped video outline You are a YouTube SEO expert. Based on the topic '<topic>', create a detailed timestamped outline for a 5–10 minute YouTube video.\n Include the main talking points, segment titles, and suggested timestamps to help with YouTube chapters and better viewer retention Prompt #11Create a landing page copy for a target industry Write landing page copy targeting companies in the '<insert industry>' sector. Highlight pain points, relevant use cases, and feature a compelling CTA.\n Prompt #12Draft a LinkedIn InMail for ABM outreach Write a professional LinkedIn InMail message to connect with a decision-maker at '<insert company name>'. Mention mutual interests, value props, and a soft CTA. Prompt #13Generate ad copy for a personalized ABM campaign Write 2–3 variations of personalized ad copy for an ABM campaign targeting '<insert account type or industry>'. Focus on relevance, urgency, and conversion. Prompt #14Research for trending topics.  What are some trending topics I can write about for a blog on X? Can you group them into different topic clusters? Prompt #15Headline for a blog Write a catchy headline about X under 30 characters Prompt #16Writing a business email Improve my business email: [paste your email here];. Make it sound polite. Make it sound smart. Output should be concise. Avoid passive voice Prompt #17Writing a newsletter.  Write a newsletter in this format (and I provide one or two examples) Prompt #18Personalize a case study for a target client Rewrite this generic case study to personalize it for '<insert company>', focusing on their niche, use case, and desired outcomes with '<insert product>'. Prompt #19Researching keywords Brainstorm 5 top keywords that I can use for a page on X based on global search volume Prompt #20Create a marketing strategy for a new product Write a comprehensive marketing strategy to launch \"<insert product>\". Here are the details ‘<target audience, key channels, positioning, messaging, and KPIs>’. Prompt #21Plan a content calendar around awareness days Create a 2-week calendar using relevant upcoming awareness days for '<insert niche or region>'. Include content ideas tied to each day. Prompt #22Draft a caption for a product teaser Write a playful and curiosity-building caption teasing the launch of '<insert product or feature>'.\n Use emojis or line breaks for style and end with a line like 'Can you guess what's coming?'\n Prompt #23Write a caption for a behind-the-scenes post Write a playful or insightful caption to show what's happening behind the scenes at '<insert project/event/team>'. Invite comments or reactions.\n Prompt #24Write a Google Search Ad for a product Write a Google Search Ad for '<insert product or service>', including headline options, descriptions, and a strong CTA. Keep it keyword-focused ‘<keyword>’ and within character limits ’<range of character limits>’. Prompt #25Write a bonus offer email for affiliates Write an email offering an exclusive bonus ‘<bonus>’ for people who buy '<insert product>' through an affiliate link ‘<link>’. Keep it persuasive. Prompt #26Repurpose blog content into social posts Take this blog post: '<insert blog title or link>' and turn it into 5 different social posts for a content calendar. Include post format, caption, and platform suggestions.\n Prompt #27Write a behind-the-scenes post caption Write an engaging caption for a behind-the-scenes Instagram post showing '<insert team/project/event>'.\n Make it authentic, showcase personality, and add a light CTA like 'Drop a 👀 if you want more BTS!'\n Prompt #28Write a 'Myth vs. Fact' post caption Write a caption for a 'Myth vs. Fact' Instagram post about '<insert industry topic>'.\n Clarify the myth, debunk it with facts, and encourage users to save or share it with someone who needs to know. Prompt #29Create a Facebook ad for a product launch Write a Facebook ad copy for launching '<insert product details>' with keyword ‘<keyword>’, including a compelling hook, benefit-driven description, and a CTA. Suggest an image or video idea too. Prompt #30Suggest a YouTube thumbnail headline You are a YouTube SEO expert. Suggest 3–5 bold and clickable thumbnail text ideas for a YouTube video on '<topic>'.\n Keep them under 6 words each, emotionally charged, and designed to boost click-through rate without misleading viewers.\n Prompt #31Generate a community post promoting the video You are a YouTube SEO expert. Write a YouTube Community post promoting a new video titled '<video title>'.\n Include a strong hook, a short summary, and 1–2 hashtags to boost visibility in user feeds and encourage click-through.\n Prompt #32Fill content gaps in a social calendar Given this partial calendar: '<paste current plan or key themes>', suggest 5 content ideas to fill topic or format gaps. Focus on variety and engagement. Prompt #33Create a testimonial post caption Write a caption to go with a customer testimonial about '<insert product or service>'.\n Make it short, emotionally resonant, and use the customer quote as a hook or centerpiece. Prompt #34Generate schema-ready product FAQs You are an SEO expert. Write 3–5 product-related FAQs for '<product name>' that address common buyer questions.\n Format them to work with FAQ schema and use these keywords ‘<keywords>’ to support search rankings and drive qualified traffic.\n Prompt #35Write alt text for product images You are an SEO expert. Suggest keyword-rich, descriptive alt text for the following product images:\n ‘<insert image descriptions or proper file names>’\n Ensure accessibility, reinforce product details, and support image SEO without keyword stuffing.\n Prompt #36Create a caption to promote an event or webinar Write a short and clear caption announcing '<insert event/webinar>'. Include the date ‘<date>’, why people should attend, and a link or CTA to sign up.\n Prompt #37Write SEO Optimized FAQ  Act as an SEO specialist. Craft a set of well-optimized and informative frequently asked questions (FAQ) for a specific [product or service] that provides value to the customers and also assists in improving search engine ranking. Start with researching the common queries that customers may have about the [product or service]. Then, create concise and relevant answers that cater to the searchers' intent and align with the targeted keywords. Make sure to use structured data markup to assist search engines in displaying relevant rich snippets significantly. Additionally, provide internal linking that directs the user toward the main pages of the website. Lastly, review the FAQ's periodically and refine it as needed to provide the most comprehensive and up-to-date information to customers while optimizing them for higher search engine visibility. Prompt #38Create a follow-up email after a LinkedIn touchpoint Write a follow-up email for someone from '<insert company>' who interacted with your LinkedIn content. Reference the interaction and suggest a meeting or resource. Prompt #39Generate subject lines for ABM email outreach Write 5 subject line options for an account-based marketing outreach email to '<insert target persona>' at '<insert company>'. Make them curiosity-piquing and relevant. Prompt #40Write a customer persona for a marketing plan Create a detailed customer persona for \"<insert product or brand>\", including these details ‘<demographics, goals, pain points, buying triggers, and preferred channels>’. Our creator partner Isabella Bedoya Our brand partner Get email insights and latest prompts in your inbox. Submit your prompt and help the community Brought to you by You might also like Enter with an idea. Exit with a winning email campaign. Exit with a winning email campaign. Brainstorm email campaign ideas with Mailmodo’s AI assistant Build precise segments in seconds with AI segmentation Generate ready-to-use email templates with AI Experience true AI email marketing automation with Mailmodo Trusted by 10000+ brands",
