ports Zoom, Google Meet, and Microsoft Teams through bot-based recording. For other meeting platforms, MeetGeek can still capture the conversation using the desktop app or browser extension. This means you can record virtually any online meeting, even when the platform is not supported by the bot directly. In-person meetings are supported through the mobile app or desktop app, and hybrid meetings are supported as well. If part of the team is in the room and others join online, you can use the local recorder that best fits the situation. Yes. You can create custom summary templates for different meeting types, such as sales calls, standups, interviews, client reviews, hiring conversations, or leadership meetings. Each template can structure the output around the information that matters most to your team, so MeetGeek does not just summarize the meeting — it produces the kind of structured output your workflow needs. Yes. MeetGeek automatically identifies and labels speakers in the transcript, so quotes, action items, insights, and key moments can be attributed to the right person. This makes transcripts easier to review and helps teams understand who said what, who committed to what, and where follow-up is needed. Yes. Your meeting history is indexed and searchable by keyword, speaker, topic, date, and other meeting properties, depending on your plan and retention settings. You can also search in a conversational way using AI chat. Instead of only filtering manually, you can ask questions across one or multiple past meetings, such as “What did this customer say about pricing?” or “What blockers came up in my last calls with this account?” Yes. You can configure sharing rules so MeetGeek automatically sends meeting summaries to participants, selected teammates, Slack channels, or connected tools after the meeting ends. This lets each team define its own follow-up flow, so sales calls, standups, customer interviews, leadership meetings, and internal reviews can each be routed differently. Yes. You can upload existing audio or video recordings and MeetGeek will generate a transcript, summary, highlights, and action items, just like it does for live meetings. This is useful when a meeting was recorded elsewhere, when you want to process legacy recordings, or when the conversation happened outside your normal MeetGeek setup. The mobile app is useful for in-person meetings, field conversations, client visits, interviews, walk-and-talk discussions, and on-the-go review. You can record conversations directly from your phone, access transcripts and summaries, review past meetings, and keep meeting intelligence available even when you are away from your desk. Some MeetGeek capabilities are cross-app, so your workflow can move between web, desktop, browser, and mobile depending on the situation. Yes. MeetGeek identifies commitments, task assignments, follow-up promises, decisions, and next steps from the conversation. Action items can be reviewed inside MeetGeek, attributed to the right person when possible, and pushed into connected tools so meeting decisions can become actual work instead of staying buried in a transcript. MeetGeek combines proprietary speech recognition technology with frontier AI models to deliver accurate transcription, structured summarization, contextual insights, and intelligent meeting analysis. The platform is designed for business use and operates with strong privacy and compliance standards, including GDPR compliance and strict controls around customer data. MeetGeek delivers industry-leading transcription accuracy across supported languages and a wide range of accents. Accuracy depends on factors such as audio quality, background noise, speaker overlap, microphone setup, and domain-specific terminology, but MeetGeek is designed to perform reliably across real business conversations, not only ideal recording conditions. MeetGeek analyzes signals such as the meeting title, participants, conversation structure, vocabulary, and discussion flow to understand the meeting context. Based on that context, it can apply the most relevant templates, insights, and outputs, helping each meeting produce a result that fits its actual purpose. MeetGeek can surface coaching metrics such as talk-to-listen ratio, monologue length, filler word usage, engagement levels, sentiment shifts, and conversational pacing. It can also provide proactive coaching suggestions based on the specific call, helping individuals and managers understand what worked, what created friction, and what could be improved next time. You can ask MeetGeek questions about a specific meeting or across multiple meetings. For a single meeting, you might ask what was agreed, what objections came up, what the client said about pricing, or what next steps were assigned. Across multiple meetings, you can ask broader questions such as “What topics keep coming up with this customer?”, “What did I discuss with this teammate over the last month?”, or “Which objections appeared most often in recent sales calls?” This turns your meeting history into a conversational knowledge base, not just a searchable archive. MeetGeek automatically detects the language spoken during the meeting and delivers the transcript and summary in that language, supporting teams across different regions without manual setup. MeetGeek identifies moments where key decisions were made, commitments were given, important topics were raised, objections appeared, sentiment shifted, or follow-up was needed. These highlights help users review the most important parts of a meeting quickly, without having to replay the full recording or scan the entire transcript. MeetGeek can identify emotional tone and sentiment shifts during a conversation, helping teams understand where a meeting became positive, neutral, tense, uncertain, or more engaged. For deeper analysis, teams can also create dedicated prompts, templates, or skills to evaluate sentiment across one meeting or