    "content": "New chat Outfit-Finder Outfit-Finder Outfit Finder is an AI-powered photo analysis tool that looks at any outfit photo you share and figures out each clothing item and accessory in it, then hands you ready to use Google search terms so you can track down and buy every piece. Whether you spotted a look on social media, in a magazine, on the street, or in your own closet, you simply upload the image and let Outfit Finder do the detective work for you.\n\nOutfit Finder scans the photo, recognizes each garment, and reads any visible logos, labels, or text to identify brands whenever possible. It then breaks the whole look down into individual cards, one for every item, complete with a short style summary of the overall outfit. For each piece you get a clear description and two search options: one aimed at the exact product and one aimed at a similar alternative in case the original is sold out or hard to find.\n\nHere is what Outfit Finder can identify for you:\n\n- Tops such as shirts, blouses, sweaters, hoodies, and tees\n- Bottoms including jeans, trousers, skirts, and shorts\n- Outerwear like jackets, coats, and blazers\n- Footwear from sneakers to boots and sandals\n- Bags, backpacks, purses, and totes\n- Accessories such as hats, belts, watches, scarves, and sunglasses\n\nEvery item comes with color, material, pattern, and style details, plus a note on any brand clues visible in the picture. The goal is to save you hours of reverse image searching and guesswork so you can shop the exact look you love in just a few clicks.\n\nFrequently Asked Questions:\n\nQuestion: What exactly is this?\nAnswer: This is Outfit Finder, an AI-powered photo analysis tool that studies the outfit photos you share and works out which clothing items and accessories appear in them, then gives you search terms to find and buy each one.\n\nQuestion: What kind of photos work best?\nAnswer: Clear, well lit images where the clothing is fully visible work best. Full outfits and single item close ups are both supported.\n\nQuestion: Can it always name the exact brand?\nAnswer: Not always. When logos, labels, or text are visible it will try to identify the brand, but when they are not it will describe the style and offer close alternatives instead.\n\nQuestion: Are the results guaranteed to be correct?\nAnswer: No. Every identification is an AI generated suggestion, so treat the results as helpful starting points for your own shopping search. Powered by Poe. Learn more",
    "source_matches_official_url": true
  },
