    "content": "Free to start \n            Answer 10 questions. Get a real website.\n           Get a real website. \n\n           TurnCage writes it, builds it and puts it online. Answer ten questions about the work you already do and a real page appears, written and live. No editor, no blank page, no design skills. No credit card. About 10 minutes. Featured on How it works Three steps. The first one is free. You answer. We build. You keep the page either way. \n          1\n           Answer 10 questions Multiple choice, tailored to your trade. Takes about ten minutes. \n          2\n           Keep your page, free Verify your phone number and it is yours. Plus a free 90-Day Marketing Plan. \n          3\n           Upgrade when ready Starter adds 3 pages. Growth builds 10 or more, one for every service you offer. 10questions to your first page 60%of your profile, still free 19trades with a page of their own $0to see yours before deciding What you get Not a template. A finished site. The words are already in it. So are the photos, the structure and the hosting. A page per service Every service you name gets its own page to rank, instead of one bullet on a crowded page. Found on Google. Named by ChatGPT. People search, and people ask assistants. Your pages are built so both can read and recommend you. Edits by text message New price? New photo? Send a text. No dashboard, no login, nothing to learn. Enquiries hit your phone Someone fills in your form and you get a message, not another thing buried in email. Hosting is our problem Google Cloud, SSL, monitoring and maintenance included. Nothing for you to patch or renew. A domain, free for a year Your own address on either paid plan, free for year one, then renewing at cost. Go deeper: the questions, search structure, blog drafting, hosting, online store. Built for your trade No two sites alike. Ever. A plumber and a photographer never end up with the same page in different colours. Six examples, not a menu. Electrician, emergency work leads Photographer, the work leads Landscaper, seasonal services Law firm, credentials and intake Hair studio, booking above the fold Winery, tastings and events 19 trades have a page of their own These get searched for in distinctive ways. Most of our customers are in trades that are not on this list, and the questions adapt either way. Compare A generator, not a builder. A builder hands you a blank page. An agency hands you an invoice. Same job, three ways. Drag it. This is the difference. Left is what a builder gives you. Right is what 10 questions gives you. TurnCage compared with a do-it-yourself builder and a design agency. Measure TurnCage DIY builder Design agency Your time 10 minutes A weekend, often more Calls and revisions Who writes it We do, you edit You do, from scratch Extra line item See it before paying Yes, a live page Only what you built After a deposit Pages you end up with 10 or more on Growth However many you finish Whatever the quote covers Hosting and upkeep Included Yours to manage Usually a retainer First year $999 all in $300 to $800, plus your time $5,000 to $15,000 Most website builds never get finished Wix reports more than 272 million sites created across its history. Independent trackers count roughly 8 to 8.5 million live today. The rest are drafts and abandoned accounts. Total creative freedom sounds generous until you are the one making every decision, writing every word and running out of a Sunday afternoon. ~96% never go live Wix’s published creation total set against third party trackers of live sites. They are not directly comparable measures, so treat this as an order of magnitude rather than a precise figure. Word on the street What people say once it is live. Your site live for under $1,000 Growth annual is $599 plus a one-time $400 setup. That is $999 all in for year one, against $1,098 normally. Annual saves $79.89 on Starter and $240.88 on Growth Try it Free build One real page from 10 questions, yours to keep. $0 No card required Nothing is charged, ever No recurring charge 10 questions, 20% of your profile One page, live and hosted, yours to keep Verify your phone number to keep it Free 90-Day Marketing Plan Not indexed by search or assistants Carries a small TurnCage banner Just the basics Starter Three pages: home, about and contact. $399.99/year Plus a one-time $299 setup $299 setup plus $399.99 for year one Then $399.99 a year The rest of the profile your plan needs Home, about and contact on your own address Google Cloud hosting, SSL and monitoring Contact form straight to your phone Custom domain, free for year one No separate page per service Publish it Growth 10 or more pages, built to be found by search and by assistants. $599/year Plus a one-time $400 setup Normally $499 setup $400 setup plus $599 for year one Then $599 a year Everything in Starter, plus: 10 or more pages, each written separately A page for every service you name A page for every reason people choose you Structured for Google and for assistants Blog drafting from a short brief Cancel your subscription any time. The one-time setup fee covers the hard costs of building and launching your site, so it is non-refundable once the website has been created. That is exactly why the first page is free, real and live before you decide anything. Questions The things people ask first. How does this actually work? You answer ten questions about your business, all multiple choice or fill in the blank, with suggestions offered as you go. The questions are tailored to your trade. Those answers complete about twenty percent of your business profile and produce a real single page, which is yours to keep once you verify your phone number. What does a TurnCage website cost? The first page is free and stays free. Starter is a one-time $299 setup plus $399.99 a year, or $39.99 a month, for three pages: home, about and contact. Growth is a one-time $400 setup plus $599 a year, or $69.99 a month, for ten or more pages. Growth on annual billing comes to $999 in year one and $599 every year after. What is the catch with the free page? No time limit and no card required, but the free page is deliberately limited. It is one page, it carries a small TurnCage banner above the fold, and it is not indexed by search engines or AI assistants. Upgrading removes all three. Do I need design or coding skills? None at all. There is no editor, no layout to arrange and no code. You are answering questions about the business you already run, which is the same set of things a top tier agency would ask you for at the start of a project. What is in the business profile? Your business name and what you do, your offerings, your advantages and guarantees, your story, your contact details and how you prefer to be contacted, your search keywords, and how your brand should look and sound. Every part of it feeds the writing, the images and the structure of your site. Can I add more detail without paying? Yes. You can take your profile as far as sixty percent at no charge, and the extra detail produces noticeably more specific writing and imagery. The remaining questions are asked once you upgrade, and Growth asks for more than Starter because it builds more pages. Can I edit the site after it is built? Yes. Send a text message with what you want changed: a price, a photo, your opening hours. There is no dashboard to learn and no software to install. Can I cancel, and is the setup fee refundable? You can cancel your subscription at any time. The one-time setup fee covers the hard costs of building and launching the site, so it is non-refundable once the website has been created. The first page is free and live before you decide anything. Can I use my own domain name? Yes. Both paid plans include a custom domain free for the first year, and it renews at cost after that. If you already own a domain, you can point it at your TurnCage site instead. More on the full FAQ page, or just ask us. Ten minutes from now, you could be done. Answer 10 questions, keep the page, decide about the rest later. Costs nothing to find out. Build mine free No credit card. Cancel any time.",
