rand and onboard. Most agencies are live the same afternoon. 1 Connect your provider API keys Paste API keys from any of the five platforms. Connect more than one provider organisation if you run several. Telephony and concurrency mirrors your own provider account. 2 Brand your portal Upload your logo, add your domain to your client portal, and create client login. Recordings, analytics and billing all sit under your brand. 3 Create your client account and charge them Give your client their own workspace. Assign the agent, campaign and phone number, connect your Stripe account, and assign the billing plan they pay you. \"The initial setup was really quick, taking about 30 minutes to an hour.\"\n\nVerified user, Small-Business, in a G2 review dated 7 July 2026. What do you get from the platform Operate without voice-minute usage caps. VoiceAIWrapper takes no revenue share; Stripe and provider fees still apply. | VoiceAIWrapper delivers 99.9% uptime and support on every plan with published response targets. | Built for agencies that look for reliability, control and speed without compromise. Multi-provider voice AI Operate multiple agent platforms from one account Operational advantage: VoiceAIWrapper connects multiple provider accounts inside a single agency account. You can match a platform to a client need instead of forcing every client onto whichever provider you started with, and compare provider performance across the same client. Retain all core voice AI provider features. Add multiple AI providers in one account. Create multiple client portals with one account. Use voice AI provider based on client need. White label and re-bill with all supported voice AI providers. White-label client portal Give every client a portal on your own domain Brand impact: VoiceAIWrapper's client portal carries your domain, your logo and your product name. Clients see their own calls, recordings, analytics and appointments. They do not see the provider or how the service is assembled. You control exactly which sections each client can open. Add your brand to your client portal with your domain, logo, and support widget. Insert custom pages to your client portal and create portals in multiple languages. The client portal also gives your clients access to their usage and billing history. Control what your clients get to see and manage inside their respective client portal. Send email alerts to clients from your own domain. Billing Set your own pricing and collect into your own Stripe Earning potential You connect your Stripe account, create the plan your client is on, and VoiceAIWrapper charges that client on your Stripe on a recurring schedule. VoiceAIWrapper does not take a share of what you charge and does not mark up voice minutes. The provider bills those to you directly at their rates. You keep 100% of client payments without any margin sharing. Charge your clients in any way you want - one-time setup fee, subscription, usage based, overage. Payment integration handles client recurring billing, cancellations. You can also bill off-platform or via API. You can bill clients in multiple global currencies. Client onboarding Sell the service from your own site, then provision it automatically More time for sales Self-serve plans let an agency publish its voice AI offer on its own website and take a new client from checkout to a working portal without a manual build. Onboarding forms, consent settings, post-checkout redirects and notification emails all run from the agency's own domain. Publish self-serve plans and take payment on your site. Customise signup and consent settings per client. Send client onboarding invitations from your own domain. Use forms for onboarding questionnaires and surveys. Streamline the agent creation process with our agent builder. Integrations Move call data into the systems your clients already run Data portability and connections VoiceAIWrapper's campaign API adds, updates and removes contacts from any source. Forwarding webhooks push call logs, transcripts and outcomes to GoHighLevel, Make, n8n or a client's CRM. Existing provider webhooks are preserved when a campaign is created, so an agency's current automations keep working. Campaign API for contact sync from any CRM or sheet. Forwarding webhooks for call logs, transcripts and outcomes. Full API and webhook logs for debugging. Full API documentation available on request. Full API integration with all 5 provider systems. Start with the job your agency already sells You have a client and a job in mind. Start there. Each page below covers one job end to end, down to what to charge and how to rebill it. What agencies using the platform say “We explored multiple platforms before choosing VoiceAIWrapper, and from the very start they stood out as the clear choice for us. Nothing else came close in terms of quality, simplicity, and the genuine support they provide.” Blake Carter Sales and Partnerships Director, VOAI “Been using VoiceAIWrapper for months now. Exponentially changes the way I am able to go to market and serve clients. Raj and team are industry experts for any issues that happen from the greater voice AI tech stack.” Bob CEO, MNY NVR SLPS “The support team has truly gone above and beyond, jumping on calls with me multiple times, patiently walking me through the setup, and making sure I understood everything without ever rushing me. I’m not very technical, but they made the entire process easy and stress-free.” Anthony King The Branding Zone \"I can confidently say VAW sets the gold standard for customer service. What really stands out is how seriously they take feature requests. Instead of waiting months (or forever) like with most SaaS companies, VAW listens, acts fast, and actually delivers. Working with them doesn’t feel like I’m just paying for another software subscription. It truly feels like I have partners walking alongside me in my business.\" Dylan Meyer Owner, Aid Financial “Their white-label platform let us hook up our clients with a nice dashboard to connect all our Retell AI agents, and it just works smooth. What I really like is how quick they are to fix stuff and how much patience they have.” Pablo Fernandez CTO, Vressh “10 out of 10 support. They reply very quickly and even help with things beyond what they officially offer. Very reliable, always staying on top of what’s new, adding features regularly, and listening to the community.” Mike Mitchell CEO, Dialverse Who this fits, and who it does not VoiceAIWrapper is not right for everyone. Reading this before you start a trial saves you a week. For a platform-by-platform view against other white-label options, see the comparison hub. Trust signals you can inspect yourself Every trust signal on this page links to VoiceAIWrapper’s own underlying document or to the third-party page behind it, rather than asking you to take a badge on faith. SOC 2 Type 2 Independent control assurance. Read the security policy. GDPR and DPA Data-protection documentation, including a DPA with standard contractual clauses and a sub-processor list. HIPAA Healthcare deployment boundaries are documented on the HIPAA page. Calling compliance Campaign responsibility and consent rules are set out on the TCPA page. 99.9% uptime Published on the status page. Public roadmap Planned work is visible on the public roadmap. Refunds Terms are set out in the refund policy. Support In-app chat, email and scheduled calls. Private Slack on Scale and Pro. Support page. What changed recently VoiceAIWrapper publishes a customer-facing changelog. The most recent entries are summarised here and the full record is public.",
