    "content": "Pick an agent. It has its own computer. It has its own computer.   A researcher, a blog writer, an SEO auditor, a data analyst — each one gets a real Linux machine in the cloud. It browses the web, writes and runs code, installs whatever it needs and keeps your files. Ask in plain language, close the laptop, come back to finished work. No card, no invite. Log in with an email code and your machine is running in under a minute — the hub and the CLI come with the same account. the agents Pick who does the work Every one runs on its own machine, with the web, a shell and your files. Not sure which? Assistant is the default and routes for you. What you stop putting up with \"Here's how you could do it…\" It has a shell, a browser and a filesystem, so it does the steps and hands you the finished file. Every chat starts from zero Same machine every time. Your files, your installs and your setup are still there tomorrow. Close the tab and the work dies It keeps going without you. You get a notification, and the full session replays on any device. Setting an agent up eats an afternoon An email code, and it's running. Nothing to install, no API keys to collect, no config to write. octo@your-machine:~$ What a chatbot doesn't have Three surfaces, on a machine that is yours. Everything else on this page follows from them. pipedrive.com/pricing hubspot.com/pricing zoho.com/crm/pricing It opens the live web and reads it — today's prices, today's docs, not a snapshot from whenever the model was trained. sudo apt install pandoc ✓ 1 newly installed python3 compare.py ✓ wrote crms.csv in 3.2s A real Linux box with passwordless sudo. If the job needs a tool it doesn't have, it installs the tool and carries on. crms.csv 2.1K brief.md 8.4K index.html 1.2K .venv/ — Everything it makes stays put and downloads in one click. Tomorrow your files and installs are exactly where you left them. everything else it comes with The rest of the machine two boards Chat is the whole product in plain language: ask, watch it work, collect your files. Studio adds machines, terminals, workflows and the config editor. One switch in the sidebar, nothing hidden either way. per-second billing Pick a size from 1 vCPU / 2 GB. You pay for the seconds it works — idle costs about a cent an hour, and a suspended machine costs storage only. sessions, anywhere Streaming replies, tool calls and permission prompts in the browser. Every session replays in full on any device; nothing is ever lost. workflows The same multi-step pipelines the CLI runs — research, write, audit, deliver. Hand one your input, watch the steps light up, collect the result and its files. shared memory One directory per account — code index, agent memory, session history — mounted into every machine you own. Index once, use everywhere. no model keys Models come through the built-in gateway. No provider accounts, no keys to collect: log in once and every machine can think. your own image On Pro, bring a Docker image built FROM our base — your toolchain, your dependencies. We pull and verify it, and you get the exact machine you wanted. REST API Everything the panel does, scriptable with one developer key: create machines, POST prompts, stream answers, collect files. On every plan, free included. What people run here Ship from anywhere Kick off a refactor from your desk, approve the plan from your phone at lunch, review the diff on the couch. The session is the same one — the machine never moved. Agents that outlive your laptop Long-running work — big migrations, research sweeps, batch processing — keeps going when you close the lid. Come back to a finished session and a notification, not a dead process. A second machine, on demand Offload the heavy stuff: indexing a large codebase, running test suites, building containers. Your laptop stays cool; the machine does the work and suspends itself after. Try octomind in 60 seconds No install, no config, no API keys. Log in with an email code and say what you need — the machine appears behind your first message. If you like it, the CLI at home uses the same account. from cold start Working in a minute 0:00  Log in with email A code, no passwords. The first login creates your account — models work in the panel and the CLI right away, with no keys to collect. 0:20  Say what you want No setup screen. Type the job in plain language; the machine comes up behind your first message and starts working. 0:45  Collect the result Answers in the chat, everything it made in Files. Want the controls instead? Studio has machines, terminals and workflows on the same account. Prefer your own hardware? The hub and the CLI work without a machine:  octomind login  and you're running locally with the same models. Drive it from code Everything the panel does is a REST API — same shapes, same errors. One developer key ( om_… , created on the Keys page) covers machines, sessions, files and usage. Idempotent POSTs,\n\t\t\t\t\tSSE streams,  X-Request-Id  on every response. The machine-readable contract is\n\t\t\t\t\tpublic at  GET /api/v1/openapi . Available on every plan, free included. The full reference lives in the panel's Docs page. $ curl -X POST https://api.octomind.run/api/v1/machines \\ -H \"Authorization: Bearer om_…\" \\ -d '{\"name\":\"ci\",\"image\":\"base\",\"size\":\"small\"}' # hand the agent a job — answers stream back $ curl -X POST …/api/v1/machines/:id/sessions \\ -H \"Authorization: Bearer om_…\" \\ -d '{\"message\":\"run the tests, fix what fails\"}' Billing you can reason about Your code, your box, your data Sandboxed per account Every machine is its own container with its own filesystem and mount — no shared state between accounts, ever. Keys shown once API keys are sha256-stored, the plaintext shown a single time. Revoke is instant, from the panel. Your files leave with you Everything on the machine is downloadable from the Files tab whenever you want — no export tickets, no waiting. Cancel without a cliff Nothing is deleted for 30 days after you cancel. Resubscribe and everything is exactly as you left it. Bring a friend — you both win. They start with +1 GB of storage; you earn permanent storage for every friend who uses it, and matching credit bonuses when they subscribe. Invite a friend → Questions, answered straight Do I need to be a developer? No. The panel opens on Chat: you type what you want in plain language and the agent does it on its machine — browsing, writing files, running whatever it needs to. You never see a terminal unless you go looking for one. Everything it makes lands in Files, downloadable in a click. Do I need an invite? No. Invites are gone — machines are open to every account, free tier included. Sign up, create a machine, and it is running in under a minute. The model hub, the panel, and the CLI are open too: install it and run `octomind login`. What exactly is a Machine? A container that belongs to you, with octomind preinstalled. You choose the size (CPU/RAM) and the image (base, Node, Python, Rust — or your own). It runs your sessions, keeps your files, and suspends itself when idle so it costs almost nothing while you sleep. What does it cost when I am not using it? Idle machines are billed a small memory-only rate (about $0.01/hr on Small), and after a few minutes of inactivity (5 min on Free, 15 on Pro — configurable) they suspend automatically — from then on you pay storage only, $0.10 per GB-month above the 10 GB included. There is never a surprise: three live caps (4-hour, weekly, monthly) are always visible in the panel. Do I need API keys for the models? No. Models come through the built-in gateway: log in once and every machine can use them. Free models are included forever; the Pro plan unlocks the strong open coding models under generous caps; premium models (Claude, GPT) run on prepaid credits. What happens to my work if the machine suspends or I cancel? Sessions and your shared directory are durable — suspend never touches them, and every session replays in full when you come back. If you cancel Pro, nothing is deleted for 30 days — resubscribe within the grace period and everything is exactly as you left it. Your files are downloadable from the Files tab whenever you want them. Can I use my own Docker image? Yes, on Pro: build any image FROM our base (that guarantees octomind and the mount contract), push it to a public registry, and point the panel at it. We pull and verify — you get your exact toolchain. Can I drive it from code — CI, cron, my own product? Yes, on every plan. Everything the panel does is a REST API: create a machine, POST a prompt at an agent session, poll or stream the result, delete the machine. It uses its own developer keys (om_…), separate from model gateway keys — create one on the Keys page; the full reference lives on the panel Docs page. Is there a real terminal or only the chat? Both, always. Chat is the plain conversation panel. Studio is the advanced one: a full web terminal into the same container, machines, workflows and the config editor. The switch sits at the foot of the sidebar and nothing is locked behind either — shells are per-connection, but your files and sessions always persist. Sixty seconds to a working agent. Email code in, machine up, agent thinking. If it's not for you, nothing to uninstall. Open the panel →",
